cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  AI Overview Industry Study: which sources Google's AI Overview cites across
  six industries
message: If you use this dataset, please cite it.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Minel
    family-names: Gunesoglu
    affiliation: Is My Brand in AI
    email: minel@ismybrandinai.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0009-4823-6016'
abstract: >-
  Thirty "best [category]" buyer searches, five in each of six industries
  (software, consumer electronics, home and appliances, finance and insurance,
  health and personal care, auto and travel), were run once each through Google
  on 11 and 12 June 2026, with US English settings. For every AI
  Overview, each source in the panel was recorded by title or brand and given a
  site type by hand. Twenty-seven searches produced an AI Overview. Review and
  authority media appeared in 24 of the 27, vendor or retailer sites in 20, and
  Reddit in 11 (41 per cent), concentrated in experiential and purchase-advice
  questions and absent from all five consumer electronics searches. An AI
  Overview listed about 6 sources, range 2 to 10. The per-query rows and a
  script that recounts every published figure from them are included.
keywords:
  - Google AI Overviews
  - AI search
  - citation
  - generative engine optimization
  - Reddit
  - industry comparison
